<p>Do you have a grandmother? Mine is blind, and she never lets me go anywhere. I''ve almost forgotten how to talk to people. Two years ago, when I got into trouble and couldn''t be controlled, she made me sit with her. She even pinned my dress to hers, and now we sit like that every day. She knits stockings, even though she''s blind, and I sit next to her, sewing or reading aloud.</p>
<p>For two years now, we''ve been stuck like that. It''s such a strange habit. My God, how awful! No, I don''t have a grandmother like that. Well, then, if you don''t, why do you stay home all the time? Do you really want to know what kind of person I am? Yes, I do. In the strict sense of the word? In the very strictest sense of the word. Very well, I am a type.</p>
