<p>Here''s my ridiculous story. I sat beside her, put on a mockingly serious expression, and began speaking as though reading from a book. There are, Nastenka, though you might not realize it, strange little corners in Petersburg. It''s as if the same sun that shines on the rest of Petersburg doesn''t reach these spots. Instead, they seem to have a different sun, one made just for them, casting a unique light on everything.</p>
<p>In these hidden corners, my dear Nastenka, life is very different from the bustling world around us. It''s a life that seems to belong to some far-off, unknown place, not to our overly serious times. This life is a mix of the wildly imaginative and passionately idealistic, combined, unfortunately, with something drab and dull, plainly ordinary, if not downright vulgar. Wow, good heavens, what an introduction! What am I hearing?</p>
<p>Listen, Nastenka. I feel like I''ll never get tired of calling you Nastenka. Let me tell you that in these little corners strange people live, dreamers. A dreamer, if you want an exact definition, isn''t really a regular person. There''s something in between. Most of the time they settle into some hidden, unreachable corner, as if they''re trying to escape the daylight. Once they find their little spot, they stick to it like a snail, or maybe more like a tortoise, that odd creature which is both an animal and its own house.</p>
<p>Now why do you think they''re so attached to their four walls, which are always painted some dull green, dirty, gloomy, and always smelling horribly of tobacco smoke? And why, when one of their rare acquaintances visits them, because eventually they manage to drive away all their friends, why does this strange person greet them with such awkwardness? They seem embarrassed, their face changes, and they look like they''ve just committed some crime within those four walls, like they''ve been forging fake money or writing poems to send to a magazine, pretending the real poet has passed away, and they feel obligated to get the work published.</p>
