<p>It''s as if they''re trapped by the gloomy expression on their host''s face. And why does the host, in turn, seem completely lost, desperately trying to liven things up, show some charm, and talk about cheerful things like women to make the visit enjoyable? And why does this visitor, suddenly remembering some urgent task that doesn''t really exist, grab their hat and hurry to leave? They pull their hand away from their host''s overly warm handshake, as the host tries their best to express regret and salvage the failed meeting.</p>
<p>Why does the visitor chuckle on their way out, promising themselves never to visit this odd person again? And yet, at the same time, they can''t help but imagine that the host''s face, during their conversation, looked exactly like a poor kitten, caught by some mischievous children, roughly handled, scared, and teased until, utterly humiliated, it hides under a chair in the dark. There it bristles up, hisses, and washes its face with its little paws, sulking over its ordeal and glaring at the world, even at the scraps of food the kind housekeeper left for it.</p>
