<p>I expected her to break into one of her innocent, irrepressible laughs, the kind that could bring lightness to even the heaviest moment. I braced myself for it, even regretting how far I had let my confession go. Why had I opened myself up so completely? Why had I poured out what had been simmering in my heart for so long? These were thoughts I had turned over endlessly in my mind, passed judgment on long ago, and here I was reliving them as though reading from a well-rehearsed script.</p>
