<p>A strange light flickered in her eyes, a mix of astonishment, curiosity, and something I couldn''t quite define. I love you, Nastenka, I said finally, the words rushing out of me like a flood breaking through a dam. There it is. Now you know everything. Now you''ll see whether you can go on speaking to me as you did before, whether you can listen to what I have to say. I spread my arms helplessly, as if to surrender to the truth I had just confessed.</p>
<p>She stared at me for a moment, her expression unreadable. Then, to my astonishment, she said, Well, what then? Her voice was calm, even thoughtful. What of it? I knew you loved me long ago. I always knew. But I thought it was just that you simply liked me very much. Oh, dear, oh, dear! She pressed a hand to her cheek, clearly flustered. At first it was just liking, I admitted, my voice trembling.</p>
