<p>I heard they''ll be performing it again soon. &quot;Yes, we''ll go, she agreed, nodding eagerly. Then, after a moment''s thought, she added, &quot;But perhaps we should see something else this time, something new, something we haven''t seen before. &quot;Of course something else, I said quickly, realizing she was right. &quot;That will be better. I don''t know why I didn''t think of it before. And so we planned, dreaming aloud about a future that seemed as though it might begin the very next day.</p>
<p>The world felt limitless, brimming with possibilities, as though nothing could ever stand in our way. As we continued talking like this, it felt as though we were moving in a dream, swept away by a kind of joyous delirium, an intoxicating rush of emotions neither of us could fully understand. We walked without purpose, as if the paths we took were chosen not by us but by some invisible force.</p>
